quran[23]{c,v,t}:
  26,61,"So when the two parties saw each other, the companions of Musa (Moses) said: ‘Indeed we are overtaken.’"
  26,62,"He (Moses) said: ‘Certainly not! Indeed, my Lord is with me. He will guide me (to the way out).’"
  26,63,"Then We revealed to Musa (Moses): ‘Strike the sea with your staff.’ So, it split (into parts). And each part was as if it were a great mountain."
  26,64,So We brought the others (i.e. Pharaoh and his people) closer.
  26,65,We saved Musa (Moses) and all those with him.
  26,66,Then We drowned the others (i.e. Pharaoh and his people).
  26,67,"There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them were not believers."
  26,68,"And indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,69,And recite to them the story of Ibrahim (Abraham).
  26,70,When he told his (foster) father and his people: ‘What are you worshipping?’
  26,71,"They said: ‘We worship idols, and We will always remain devoted to them.’"
  26,72,He (Abraham) said: ‘Do they hear you when you call (them)?
  26,73,Or do they bring you any benefit or cause you any harm?’
  26,74,They said: ‘Rather we found our fathers doing likewise.’
  26,75,"He (Abraham) said: ‘Have you (ever) realised what you have been worshipping,"
  26,76,you and your ancestors?’
  26,77,"They are indeed my enemies. But the Lord of all worlds,"
  26,78,Who created me—He guides me.
  26,79,And He is the One Who gives me to eat and gives me to drink.
  26,80,"And when I get sick, He is the One Who cures me."
  26,81,"And Who will cause me to die, then He will bring me to life (again)."
  26,82,"And Who, I hope, will forgive me my faults on the Day of Judgement."
  26,83,"My Lord! Grant me unerring judgement (and wisdom), and join me with the righteous."
